PHYSICS SANITY SUMMARY
  [PASS] homogeneous box returns the matrix moduli (rel. err 4.5e-16) - FE machinery is correct.
  [FAIL] every FE modulus and the FE mean lie inside the Hashin-Shtrikman bounds [3696, 3766] MPa.
      -> FE exceeds the HS UPPER bound by at most 1.2%. The HS band here is only 1.9% wide (stiff shell, moderate contrast), so this is a small absolute overshoot, and it is NOT a volume-fraction artefact: the bounds above were re-evaluated at each run's voxelised vf (0.2983-0.2996 vs target 0.30) and the overshoot persists.
      -> Diagnosis: KUBC on a finite 16-sphere cell constrains the boundary to an affine displacement and so overestimates stiffness; it is an upper-bound-type estimate for THAT cell, not a realisation of the statistically isotropic infinite medium the HS bounds describe. Refining the mesh moves E towards the bound (n=16: 3807.1 -> n=24: 3795.7 MPa, -0.30%), and periodic BCs with more spheres would be expected to bring it inside. Reported as-is, not tuned.
  [PASS] |FE mean - MT| / MT = 2.8% < 25%.
  K46 microballoons (equivalent E = 5970 MPa) are stiffer than the epoxy (3000 MPa), so E rises above the matrix while density falls to 0.964 g/cm3 (matrix 1.18) - the expected syntactic-foam trade-off.
  FE (KUBC) sits above Mori-Tanaka, consistent with KUBC being an upper-bound-type estimate on a finite 16-sphere RVE; the 4-run spread (0.4% of the mean) is the mesh+realisation uncertainty, not a physical one.
